y platforms. It also provides restoration support services, digital reputation, and secure financial wellness. The company offers its products under the Norton, Avast, LifeLock, MoneyLion, Avira, AVG, ReputationDefender, and CCleaner brands. The company was formerly known as NortonLifeLock Inc. and changed its name to Gen Digital Inc. in November 2022. Gen Digital Inc. was founded in 1982 and is headquartered in Tempe, Arizona.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Vincent  Pilette | CEO, President & Chairman | Age 53 | Compensation: $3.1M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.3M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers. Each employee generates $391K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $61K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 2\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Gen Digital Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $17.7B market cap on $5.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +14% over the past three years and +3% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 8% cost of capital, a 6-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it. Gross margins of 82% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $1.5B in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 30 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.59\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, debt is moderate at 3.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, serviceable in normal conditions but worth watching through a downturn, and interest coverage runs at 3.7\u00d7.","Management returns a meaningful 5.4% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.8% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (1.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Goodwill represents 71% of total assets \u2014 a large impairment risk hanging over book value","sev":"red","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.10598413842826251},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.3% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (90% sell ratio, net $19.6M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Carries more leverage than most Technology peers \u2014 a smaller cushion for the inevitable bad year","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 35% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 66% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 33% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","12 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Travis Witteveen Sells 30,000 Shares of Gen Digital at $29.75 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/travis-witteveen-sells-30000-shares-of-gen-digital-at-2975-each","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793856825.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.296,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will Earnings Beat Change Gen Digital Stock Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-gen/gen-digital/news/will-earnings-beat-change-gen-digital-stock-narrative","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793693849.668,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.939,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Rail Deal Race: Will Genmin (ASX:GEN) Lock In Gabon Terms in Time?","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/au/commodity/iron-ore/rail-deal-race-will-genmin-asxgen-lock-in-gabon-terms-in-time","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793681220.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Gen Digital (GEN) Posts Strong Q2 Growth, Is It Still 8% Undervalued?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-gen/gen-digital/news/gen-digital-gen-posts-strong-q2-growth-is-it-still-8-underva","date":"2026-11-02","timestamp":1793591212.033,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.934,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Behavioral Patterns of GEN and Institutional Flows","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_rel